cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "szl-typesafe-triage: a deployed triage engine measured against its own formal specification"
authors:
  - family-names: Lutar
    given-names: "Stephen P."
    name-suffix: Jr.
    affiliation: "SZL Holdings"
repository-code: "https://github.com/szl-holdings/szl-typesafe-triage"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
keywords:
  - governed AI
  - measurement discipline
  - corpus contamination
  - non-compensatory aggregation
  - receipts
abstract: >
  A deterministic, receipt-bearing triage engine, reported together with the measurements that show
  where it fails: a compensatory four-axis aggregator against a non-compensatory 13-axis governance gate,
  a corpus refused by a contamination gate, and an append-only ledger of 16 retractions.
  No model is trained and no baseline is beaten.